Q: Accessing constant variables from a lambda in Visual Studio 2026 A: <p>In C++20, even if a variable is <code>constexpr</code>, if you take its address or pass an array (which decays to a pointer), it is &quot;ODR-used.&quot; This requires the variable to be captured.</p>
<pre><code>void f(const void*) {}

int main() {
    constexpr float one[1] = { 1.0f };

    // Capture the pointer to the array explicitly
    [ptr = one]() {
        f(ptr);
        f(&amp;ptr[0]);
    }();
}
</code></pre>
